{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the name of the one was Eliezer.</b> It should have said 'and the name of the second.' By way of the plain sense (peshat): this one is dedicated to his mother and that one to his father — Gershom, who was the firstborn, was dedicated to his mother, and also because she saved him from death, in the manner of what is said (Exodus 4:25): ״ותקח צפורה צר״; and Eliezer was dedicated to Moses, for he so named him on account of his deliverance." "<b>And it is possible</b> to interpret further that he used the term אחד ('one') for Eliezer because the power of multiplicity flows from the power of oneness. And since the Holy One, blessed be He, was destined to bestow the power of multiplicity upon the seed of Eliezer — who was Rehabiah — in the manner of what is said in Chronicles (1 Chronicles 23:17): ״ויהיו בני אליעזר רחביה הראש ולא היה לאליעזר בנים אחרים ובני רחביה רבו למעלה״ — and our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted ״למעלה״ as more than sixty myriad — therefore he used in him the term אחד, to indicate that multiplicity flows from the power of oneness." "<b>By way of the Midrash:</b> ״And the name of the one was Eliezer״ — R. Yossi bar R. Hanina said: When Moses ascended on high, he found the Holy One, blessed be He, engaged in the passage of the red heifer, and He was citing the halakhah in the name of Rabbi Eliezer: ״עגלה ערופה בת שנתה ופרה אדומה בת שתי שנים״. He said before Him: Master of the universe, all those above and below are Yours, and You cite the halakhah in the name of a creature of flesh and blood? He said to him: A certain righteous man is destined to arise in My world, and Eliezer is his name, and he is destined to engage in the red heifer first, and he will say, ״עגלה בת שנתה, פרה בת שתי שנים״. He said before Him: Master of the universe, may it be Your will that he be from my descendants. He said to him: By your life, he is from your descendants, as is said: ״ושם האחד אליעזר״ — and the name of that designated one is Eliezer:"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "Rabbeinu Bahya's citation '(שם ד)' refers to Exodus 4:25, the preceding chapter-and-verse context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:35.304555816Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}